WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.370
Telemetry is security-relevant data generated by systems, applications, identities, networks, endpoints, and cloud services.

2
00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:23.223
It can include audit logs, authentication logs, endpoint events, network logs, cloud activity records, vulnerability scan results, configuration snapshots, change records, tickets, incident records, and compliance evidence.

3
00:00:23.223 --> 00:00:32.272
Telemetry is the raw material of monitoring, but raw data only becomes useful when it is reliable, understandable, and available when needed.

4
00:00:32.272 --> 00:00:34.157
Source reliability matters.

5
00:00:34.157 --> 00:00:39.510
A log source that silently stops sending data can create a false sense of visibility.

6
00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:44.562
A scanner that misses important assets can distort vulnerability priorities.

7
00:00:44.562 --> 00:00:48.558
A ticket queue with inconsistent fields can weaken reporting.

8
00:00:48.558 --> 00:00:54.213
A configuration snapshot without timestamps or ownership may be hard to use as evidence.

9
00:00:54.213 --> 00:01:01.603
Monitoring programs should track the health and quality of their evidence sources, not only the events inside them.

10
00:01:01.603 --> 00:01:07.031
Retention and time synchronization are practical details with large consequences.

11
00:01:07.031 --> 00:01:13.365
Retention affects how far back investigators, auditors, and operators can reconstruct activity.

12
00:01:13.365 --> 00:01:19.020
Time synchronization affects whether events from different systems can be correlated.

13
00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:33.497
If authentication logs, cloud activity logs, endpoint events, and tickets all use inconsistent clocks or short retention windows, the organization may struggle to understand what happened during an incident or audit review.

14
00:01:33.497 --> 00:01:37.116
Evidence should be current, traceable, and reviewable.

15
00:01:37.116 --> 00:01:41.263
Current means it reflects the system as it actually operates now.

16
00:01:41.263 --> 00:01:48.577
Traceable means a reviewer can connect evidence back to the asset, control, owner, event, or decision it supports.

17
00:01:48.577 --> 00:01:53.026
Reviewable means it is understandable to the people who need to use it.

18
00:01:53.026 --> 00:02:00.792
Continuous monitoring improves when evidence quality is treated as part of the security program, not as an afterthought.
